# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What are multi-product formulas? {#what-are-multi-product-formulas}"
msgstr "What are multi-product formulas? {#what-are-multi-product-formulas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When simulating quantum systems on a quantum computer, a central task is to approximate the time-evolution operator $e^{-iHt}$ for a Hamiltonian $H$. The standard approach uses *product formulas* (PFs), also known as Trotter-Suzuki decompositions. These decompose $H = \\sum_{a=1}^d F_a$ into terms whose individual unitaries $e^{-iF_a t}$ are efficient to implement, and then approximate the full evolution as an ordered product of these simpler unitaries.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ginagaya ang mga quantum system sa isang quantum computer, isang sentral na gawain ay ang pag-approximate ng time-evolution operator $e^{-iHt}$ para sa isang Hamiltonian $H$. Ang standard approach ay gumagamit ng *product formulas* (PFs), na kilala rin bilang Trotter-Suzuki decompositions. Dinedekompos nito ang $H = \\sum_{a=1}^d F_a$ sa mga terms kung saan ang kani-kaniyang unitaries na $e^{-iF_a t}$ ay episyenteng maipapatupad, at pagkatapos ay ina-approximate ang buong evolution bilang isang ordered product ng mga simpleng unitary na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first-order product formula (Lie-Trotter) is:\n"
msgstr "Ang first-order product formula (Lie-Trotter) ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"S_1(t) := \\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"S_1(t) := \\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which incurs a quadratic error: $S_1(t) = e^{-iHt} + \\mathcal{O}(t^2)$. Higher-order symmetric formulas $S_{2\\chi}(t)$, where $\\chi$ labels the order of the symmetric product formula (see Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references)), converge faster as $e^{-iHt} + \\mathcal{O}(t^{2\\chi+1})$, but at the cost of deeper circuits per step.\n"
msgstr "na nagdudulot ng quadratic error: $S_1(t) = e^{-iHt} + \\mathcal{O}(t^2)$. Ang mga higher-order symmetric formula na $S_{2\\chi}(t)$, kung saan ang $\\chi$ ay nagla-label sa order ng symmetric product formula (tingnan ang Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references)), ay kumokombergehe nang mas mabilis bilang $e^{-iHt} + \\mathcal{O}(t^{2\\chi+1})$, ngunit sa halaga ng mas malalim na circuits bawat hakbang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To reduce the error at a *fixed* order $\\chi$, one usually splits the total evolution time $t$ into $k$ smaller Trotter steps. Each step approximates $e^{-iHt/k}$ by a product formula and the steps are concatenated:\n"
msgstr "Upang mabawasan ang error sa isang *fixed* na order $\\chi$, karaniwang hinahati ang kabuuang evolution time $t$ sa $k$ na mas maliliit na Trotter steps. Bawat hakbang ay ina-approximate ang $e^{-iHt/k}$ ng isang product formula at ang mga hakbang ay pinagsasama-sama:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-iHt} \\approx \\left[S_{2\\chi}(t/k)\\right]^k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-iHt} \\approx \\left[S_{2\\chi}(t/k)\\right]^k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a $2\\chi$-order symmetric formula the residual Trotter error then scales as $\\mathcal{O}\\!\\left(t^{2\\chi+1} / k^{2\\chi}\\right)$. So increasing $k$ rapidly suppresses the Trotter error &mdash; but it also linearly deepens the circuit, and on noisy hardware that means more accumulated gate noise. This tension between **Trotter error (favors larger $k$)** and **hardware noise (favors smaller $k$)** is precisely what multi-product formulas are designed to resolve. Note that MPFs are about combining results from *different choices of $k$* at a fixed order $\\chi$ &mdash; they do not change the order of the underlying product formula.\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang $2\\chi$-order symmetric formula, ang residual Trotter error ay nagsi-scale bilang $\\mathcal{O}\\!\\left(t^{2\\chi+1} / k^{2\\chi}\\right)$. Kaya ang pagtaas ng $k$ ay mabilis na sumusupress sa Trotter error &mdash; ngunit ito rin ay linear na nagpapalalim sa circuit, at sa noisy hardware nangangahulugan ito ng mas maraming naiipong gate noise. Ang tension na ito sa pagitan ng **Trotter error (pumapabor sa mas malaking $k$)** at **hardware noise (pumapabor sa mas maliit na $k$)** ang eksaktong disenyo ng multi-product formulas upang lutasin. Tandaan na ang MPFs ay tungkol sa pagsasama-sama ng mga resulta mula sa *magkakaibang pagpili ng $k$* sa isang fixed order $\\chi$ &mdash; hindi nito binabago ang order ng underlying product formula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Multi-product formulas (MPFs)** [\\[1\\]](#references) construct a *weighted linear combination* of expectation values obtained from several shallower Trotter circuits, each using a different number of Trotter steps $k_1, k_2, \\ldots, k_r$ (a set of $r$ step counts):\n"
msgstr "Ang **Multi-product formulas (MPFs)** [\\[1\\]](#references) ay bumubuo ng isang *weighted linear combination* ng expectation values na nakuha mula sa ilang mas mabababaw na Trotter circuits, bawat isa ay gumagamit ng ibang bilang ng Trotter steps na $k_1, k_2, \\ldots, k_r$ (isang set ng $r$ na step counts):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A \\rangle_{\\text{MPF}}(t) = \\sum_{j=1}^r x_j \\, \\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle A \\rangle_{\\text{MPF}}(t) = \\sum_{j=1}^r x_j \\, \\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t)$ is the expectation value of an observable $A$ at time $t$ estimated from a Trotter circuit with $k_j$ steps, and the coefficients $\\{x_j\\}_{j=1}^r$ are chosen so that the leading Trotter-error terms in the combination cancel. We will revisit this expression in [Step 4](#small-scale-step-4), where we evaluate it explicitly to combine our Trotter results. The key practical point is that the deepest circuit in the MPF only needs $k_{\\max}$ steps, which is much smaller than the single $k$ that would be required to reach the same effective Trotter error directly. The shallower circuits make the MPF approach better suited to noisy hardware.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t)$ ay ang expectation value ng isang observable $A$ sa oras $t$ na na-estimate mula sa isang Trotter circuit na may $k_j$ steps, at ang mga coefficient na $\\{x_j\\}_{j=1}^r$ ay pinipili upang mag-cancel ang mga leading Trotter-error terms sa combination. Babalikan natin ang expression na ito sa [Step 4](#small-scale-step-4), kung saan susuriin natin ito nang explicit upang pagsamahin ang ating mga resultang Trotter. Ang pangunahing praktikal na punto ay ang pinakamalalim na circuit sa MPF ay nangangailangan lamang ng $k_{\\max}$ na steps, na mas maliit kaysa sa iisang $k$ na kakailanganin upang maabot direkta ang parehong effective Trotter error. Ang mas mabababaw na circuits ang gumagawa sa MPF approach na mas angkop para sa noisy hardware.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "How are the coefficients determined? {#how-are-the-coefficients-determined}"
msgstr "How are the coefficients determined? {#how-are-the-coefficients-determined}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are two families of MPF coefficients:\n"
msgstr "May dalawang pamilya ng MPF coefficients:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Static coefficients** are independent of the Hamiltonian, the initial state, and the evolution time. They are found by solving a linear system $Ax = b$ that enforces cancellation of the leading Trotter error terms. For a set of Trotter steps $\\{k_j\\}_{j=1}^r$ used with a $2\\chi$-order symmetric product formula, expanding the Trotter error in inverse powers of $k_j$ leads to constraint equations of the form:\n"
msgstr "Ang **Static coefficients** ay independiyente sa Hamiltonian, sa initial state, at sa evolution time. Nakukuha ang mga ito sa pamamagitan ng paglutas ng isang linear system na $Ax = b$ na nag-eenforce ng cancellation ng leading Trotter error terms. Para sa isang set ng Trotter steps na $\\{k_j\\}_{j=1}^r$ na ginamit kasama ng isang $2\\chi$-order symmetric product formula, ang pag-expand ng Trotter error sa inverse powers ng $k_j$ ay humahantong sa constraint equations ng anyo:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{j=1}^r x_j = 1, \\quad \\sum_{j=1}^r \\frac{x_j}{k_j^{\\eta_n}} = 0 \\quad (n = 0, \\ldots, r-2),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{j=1}^r x_j = 1, \\quad \\sum_{j=1}^r \\frac{x_j}{k_j^{\\eta_n}} = 0 \\quad (n = 0, \\ldots, r-2),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the integer exponents $\\{\\eta_n\\}$ are the orders of the successive Trotter-error terms for the chosen product formula. For a *symmetric* $2\\chi$-order PF, the leading error in $\\left[S_{2\\chi}(t/k)\\right]^k$ scales as $1/k^{2\\chi}$, with subsequent corrections at $1/k^{2\\chi+2}, 1/k^{2\\chi+4}, \\ldots$ &mdash; so the exponents are $\\eta_n = 2\\chi + 2n$. For non-symmetric PFs, both odd and even powers contribute and $\\eta_n = 2\\chi + n$. See Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) for the full derivation. The first equation in the system above ensures unbiasedness (the MPF reproduces the exact expectation value in the $k_j \\to \\infty$ limit), and the remaining $r-1$ equations successively cancel the first $r-1$ Trotter-error terms. When the resulting $L_1$-norm $\\|x\\|_1$ is too large (which amplifies sampling noise), you can instead solve an approximate optimization that caps $\\|x\\|_1$ while minimizing $\\|Ax - b\\|$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang mga integer exponent na $\\{\\eta_n\\}$ ay ang mga order ng magkakasunod na Trotter-error terms para sa napiling product formula. Para sa isang *symmetric* $2\\chi$-order PF, ang leading error sa $\\left[S_{2\\chi}(t/k)\\right]^k$ ay nagsi-scale bilang $1/k^{2\\chi}$, na may kasunod na mga correction sa $1/k^{2\\chi+2}, 1/k^{2\\chi+4}, \\ldots$ &mdash; kaya ang mga exponent ay $\\eta_n = 2\\chi + 2n$. Para sa non-symmetric PFs, kapwa ang odd at even powers ay nag-aambag at $\\eta_n = 2\\chi + n$. Tingnan ang Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) para sa buong derivation. Ang unang equation sa system sa itaas ay tinitiyak ang unbiasedness (ginagaya ng MPF ang eksaktong expectation value sa $k_j \\to \\infty$ limit), at ang natitirang $r-1$ na equations ay magkakasunod na kinakansela ang unang $r-1$ na Trotter-error terms. Kapag ang resultang $L_1$-norm na $\\|x\\|_1$ ay masyadong malaki (na nagpapalakas sa sampling noise), maaari kang lumutas sa halip ng isang approximate optimization na nagli-limit sa $\\|x\\|_1$ habang minamaliit ang $\\|Ax - b\\|$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Dynamic coefficients** [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references) additionally depend on the Hamiltonian, initial state, and evolution time $t$. They minimize the Frobenius-norm distance between the true time-evolved state and the MPF approximation:\n"
msgstr "Ang **Dynamic coefficients** [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references) ay nakadepende rin sa Hamiltonian, sa initial state, at sa evolution time na $t$. Minimize nila ang Frobenius-norm distance sa pagitan ng totoong time-evolved state at ng MPF approximation:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\|\\rho(t) - \\mu^D(t)\\|_F^2 = 1 + \\sum_{i,j} M_{ij}(t)\\, x_i(t)\\, x_j(t) - 2\\sum_i L_i(t)\\, x_i(t),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\|\\rho(t) - \\mu^D(t)\\|_F^2 = 1 + \\sum_{i,j} M_{ij}(t)\\, x_i(t)\\, x_j(t) - 2\\sum_i L_i(t)\\, x_i(t),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $M_{ij}(t) = \\mathrm{Tr}[\\rho_{k_i}(t)\\,\\rho_{k_j}(t)]$ is the Gram matrix of overlaps between Trotter-evolved states for different step counts $k_i, k_j$, and $L_i(t) = \\mathrm{Tr}[\\rho(t)\\,\\rho_{k_i}(t)]$ measures overlap with the (approximate) exact state. In this tutorial these quantities are computed efficiently using tensor-network methods, specifically the TeNPy-based backends in `qiskit_addon_mpf`.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $M_{ij}(t) = \\mathrm{Tr}[\\rho_{k_i}(t)\\,\\rho_{k_j}(t)]$ ay ang Gram matrix ng overlaps sa pagitan ng mga Trotter-evolved states para sa iba't ibang step counts na $k_i, k_j$, at ang $L_i(t) = \\mathrm{Tr}[\\rho(t)\\,\\rho_{k_i}(t)]$ ay sumusukat ng overlap sa (approximate) eksaktong state. Sa tutorial na ito, ang mga dami na ito ay kinokompyut nang episyente gamit ang tensor-network methods, partikular ang mga TeNPy-based backend sa `qiskit_addon_mpf`.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "When to use MPFs {#when-to-use-mpfs}"
msgstr "When to use MPFs {#when-to-use-mpfs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "MPFs are most beneficial when:\n"
msgstr "Ang MPFs ay pinaka-kapaki-pakinabang kapag:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuit depth is the bottleneck.** If hardware noise limits the depth you can run, use MPFs to achieve higher effective Trotter accuracy from shallower circuits.\n"
msgstr "**Ang circuit depth ang bottleneck.** Kung ang hardware noise ang naglilimita sa depth na maaari mong patakbuhin, gamitin ang MPFs upang makamit ang mas mataas na effective Trotter accuracy mula sa mas mabababaw na circuits.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**You need accurate expectation values, not full state preparation.** MPFs operate at the level of expectation values &mdash; they combine classical numbers, not quantum states. They are therefore ideal for observable estimation when using the Estimator primitive.\n"
msgstr "**Kailangan mo ng tumpak na expectation values, hindi buong state preparation.** Ang MPFs ay gumagana sa antas ng expectation values &mdash; pinagsasama nila ang mga classical number, hindi quantum states. Kaya't ideal ang mga ito para sa observable estimation kapag gumagamit ng Estimator primitive.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**You combine a modest number of Trotter-step counts.** Typically combining $r = 3$&ndash;$5$ different step counts $k_j$ is sufficient to cancel several leading Trotter-error terms while keeping $\\|x\\|_1$ manageable.\n"
msgstr "**Pinagsasama mo ang katamtamang bilang ng Trotter-step counts.** Karaniwan, ang pagsasama ng $r = 3$&ndash;$5$ na magkakaibang step counts na $k_j$ ay sapat na upang kanselahin ang ilang leading Trotter-error terms habang pinapanatiling manageable ang $\\|x\\|_1$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "When MPFs might not help {#when-mpfs-might-not-help}"
msgstr "Kapag hindi nakakatulong ang MPFs {#when-mpfs-might-not-help}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Very short evolution times.** When $t$ is small enough that a single low-order Trotter formula is already accurate, the overhead of running multiple circuits is unnecessary.\n"
msgstr "**Napakaikling oras ng ebolusyon.** Kapag maliit na ang $t$ na sapat na ang isang mababang-order na Trotter formula ay tama na, ang overhead ng pagpapatakbo ng maraming circuit ay hindi na kailangan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**State-preparation tasks.** MPFs produce a corrected *expectation value*, not a corrected quantum state. If you need the actual time-evolved state (for example, as input to another quantum subroutine), MPFs do not apply.\n"
msgstr "**Mga gawain sa paghahanda ng estado.** Ang mga MPF ay gumagawa ng naitamang *expectation value*, hindi naitamang quantum state. Kung kailangan mo ang aktwal na time-evolved na estado (halimbawa, bilang input sa isa pang quantum subroutine), hindi angkop ang MPFs.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trotter-step counts that violate the convergence regime.** The static-coefficient derivation expands each individual $\\left[S_{2\\chi}(t/k_j)\\right]^{k_j}$ as a series in $t/k_j$; this expansion only converges well when $t/k_{\\min} \\lesssim 1$. If $k_{\\min}$ is chosen too small for the given $t$, the shallowest circuit is far outside the perturbative regime, the higher-order error terms that the MPF leaves uncanceled become large, and the cancellation can require large coefficients. The $L_1$-norm $\\|x\\|_1$ is the practical diagnostic: when $\\|x\\|_1 \\gg 1$, the sampling overhead $\\propto \\|x\\|_1^2$ might outweigh the Trotter-error reduction. See the [guide on choosing Trotter steps](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html) for details.\n"
msgstr "**Mga bilang ng Trotter-step na lumalabag sa convergence regime.** Ang static-coefficient derivation ay nagpapalawak ng bawat indibidwal na $\\left[S_{2\\chi}(t/k_j)\\right]^{k_j}$ bilang isang series sa $t/k_j$; ang expansion na ito ay mahusay lang nagko-converge kapag $t/k_{\\min} \\lesssim 1$. Kung masyadong maliit ang $k_{\\min}$ na napili para sa ibinigay na $t$, ang pinakamababaw na circuit ay malayo sa perturbative regime, ang mga higher-order error terms na hindi na-cancel ng MPF ay nagiging malaki, at ang cancellation ay maaaring mangailangan ng malalaking coefficients. Ang $L_1$-norm na $\\|x\\|_1$ ay ang praktikal na diagnostic: kapag $\\|x\\|_1 \\gg 1$, ang sampling overhead na $\\propto \\|x\\|_1^2$ ay maaaring mas malaki kaysa sa pagbawas ng Trotter-error. Tingnan ang [gabay sa pagpili ng Trotter steps](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/choose_trotter_steps.html) para sa detalye.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What this tutorial covers {#what-this-tutorial-covers}"
msgstr "Ano ang sinasaklaw ng tutorial na ito {#what-this-tutorial-covers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial walks through an end-to-end MPF workflow in two stages. First, a **small-scale simulator example** (10-qubit Heisenberg chain) demonstrates how to set up the problem, compute static and dynamic MPF coefficients, and compare the resulting expectation values against exact diagonalization. Then, a **large-scale hardware example** (50-qubit XXZ chain) shows how to transpile, execute on IBM Quantum hardware with error mitigation, and post-process results using the MPF coefficients. Throughout, we use the `qiskit_addon_mpf` package alongside standard Qiskit tools.\n"
msgstr "Ang tutorial na ito ay dumadaan sa isang end-to-end MPF workflow sa dalawang yugto. Una, isang **maliit na halimbawa gamit ang simulator** (10-qubit Heisenberg chain) na nagpapakita kung paano itakda ang problema, kalkulahin ang static at dynamic na MPF coefficients, at ikumpara ang resultang expectation values laban sa exact diagonalization. Pagkatapos, isang **malaking halimbawa gamit ang hardware** (50-qubit XXZ chain) na nagpapakita kung paano mag-transpile, magpatakbo sa IBM Quantum hardware gamit ang error mitigation, at i-post-process ang mga resulta gamit ang MPF coefficients. Sa buong tutorial, ginagamit natin ang `qiskit_addon_mpf` package kasama ng standard na Qiskit tools.\n"

