# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below we collect *all* the package imports used throughout this tutorial in a single cell. We also define a `CollectAndCollapse` transpiler pass that fuses adjacent `rxx` and `ryy` rotations into a single `XXPlusYYGate`. This pass is applied both during circuit construction in Step 1 (to keep the gate count low) and indirectly when we extract the layered structure for the dynamic MPF in Step 4 (TeNPy expects two-qubit gates, not pairs of unfused rotations).\n"
msgstr "Sa ibaba ay tinipon natin ang *lahat* ng package imports na ginamit sa buong tutorial na ito sa isang cell. Nagtatakda rin tayo ng `CollectAndCollapse` transpiler pass na pinagsasama-sama ang magkatabing `rxx` at `ryy` rotations sa iisang `XXPlusYYGate`. Ang pass na ito ay inilalapat parehong sa panahon ng pagbuo ng circuit sa Hakbang 1 (upang mapanatiling mababa ang bilang ng gate) at hindi tuwiran kapag kinuha natin ang layered structure para sa dynamic MPF sa Hakbang 4 (inaasahan ng TeNPy ang two-qubit gates, hindi pares ng unfused rotations).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Maliit na halimbawa gamit ang simulator {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We begin with a 10-qubit Heisenberg model on a line, using the Néel state $\\vert 0101\\ldots01 \\rangle$ as the initial state. The Hamiltonian is:\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula tayo sa isang 10-qubit Heisenberg model sa isang linya, gamit ang Néel state na $\\vert 0101\\ldots01 \\rangle$ bilang paunang estado. Ang Hamiltonian ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Heis}} = J \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1} \\left(X_i X_{i+1} + Y_i Y_{i+1} + Z_i Z_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}_{\\text{Heis}} = J \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1} \\left(X_i X_{i+1} + Y_i Y_{i+1} + Z_i Z_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J$ is the nearest-neighbor coupling strength. We measure the ZZ correlator $Z_{L/2-1} Z_{L/2}$ on a pair of qubits in the middle of the chain, and use Trotter steps $k_j = [1, 2, 4]$ with a second-order product formula.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $J$ ay ang nearest-neighbor coupling strength. Sinusukat natin ang ZZ correlator na $Z_{L/2-1} Z_{L/2}$ sa isang pares ng qubits sa gitna ng chain, at gumagamit ng Trotter steps na $k_j = [1, 2, 4]$ na may second-order product formula.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build Trotter circuits {#build-trotter-circuits}"
msgstr "Bumuo ng mga Trotter circuit {#build-trotter-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We create the circuits implementing the approximate Trotter time-evolutions for each time point and each Trotter step count. The `CollectAndCollapse` pass defined in the Setup section collects XX and YY rotations into single XX+YY gates, to prepare for more efficient tensor-network simulation later.\n"
msgstr "Gumagawa tayo ng mga circuit na nagpapatupad ng tinatayang Trotter time-evolutions para sa bawat time point at bawat Trotter step count. Ang `CollectAndCollapse` pass na itinakda sa seksyon ng Setup ay pinagsasama-sama ang XX at YY rotations sa iisang XX+YY gates, upang maghanda para sa mas mahusay na tensor-network simulation sa susunod.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/multi-product-formula/extracted-outputs/c7ee61e7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/multi-product-formula/extracted-outputs/c7ee61e7-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the small-scale example we target the Aer simulator. Two transformations happen before the circuits are ready to execute:\n"
msgstr "Para sa maliit na halimbawa, tina-target natin ang Aer simulator. Dalawang transformation ang nangyayari bago handa nang isagawa ang mga circuit:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Gate collection at the Hamiltonian-simulation level.** In the Setup cell we built a `CollectAndCollapse` pass that fuses adjacent `rxx` and `ryy` rotations into a single `XXPlusYYGate`. We already applied this pass when we built the Trotter circuits in Step 1 (the `pm.run(...)` call). This both reduces the two-qubit gate count and produces a structure that is more amenable to tensor-network simulation for the dynamic-coefficient computation later.\n"
msgstr "**Pagkolekta ng gate sa antas ng Hamiltonian-simulation.** Sa Setup cell binuo natin ang isang `CollectAndCollapse` pass na pinagsasama-sama ang magkatabing `rxx` at `ryy` rotations sa iisang `XXPlusYYGate`. Nailapat na natin ang pass na ito noong binuo natin ang mga Trotter circuit sa Hakbang 1 (ang `pm.run(...)` call). Binabawasan nito ang bilang ng two-qubit gate at gumagawa ng structure na mas angkop para sa tensor-network simulation para sa dynamic-coefficient computation sa susunod.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Lowering to the simulator's ISA.** Below we run the Qiskit preset pass manager at `optimization_level=3` to lower each Trotter circuit to the simulator's instruction-set architecture (ISA).\n"
msgstr "**Pagbaba sa ISA ng simulator.** Sa ibaba, pinapatakbo natin ang Qiskit preset pass manager sa `optimization_level=3` upang ibaba ang bawat Trotter circuit sa instruction-set architecture (ISA) ng simulator.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the small-scale example we run the ISA-lowered Trotter circuits through the `EstimatorV2` primitive backed by Aer. Doing so gives us a *noiseless* reference value for each $(k_j, t)$ pair &mdash; these are the $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t)$ values that the MPF will combine in Step 4. We sweep over evolution times so that we can later plot the full time-series curve of each individual product formula and of the MPF.\n"
msgstr "Para sa maliit na halimbawa, pinapatakbo natin ang mga ISA-lowered Trotter circuits sa pamamagitan ng `EstimatorV2` primitive na suportado ng Aer. Sa paggawa nito, nakakakuha tayo ng *walang ingay* na reference value para sa bawat $(k_j, t)$ pares &mdash; ito ang mga $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t)$ values na pagsasamahin ng MPF sa Hakbang 4. Sinusuri natin ang iba't ibang oras ng ebolusyon upang mas maaari nating i-plot ang buong time-series curve ng bawat indibidwal na product formula at ng MPF.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"small-scale-step-4\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na klasikal na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4 is where the MPF is actually constructed. Even though the coefficients $x_j$ are *computed* here (and, for the dynamic variant, this computation can be intensive), conceptually they are a classical recipe for combining the quantum measurements from Step 3 into a single corrected expectation value &mdash; so we treat the whole coefficient and combination workflow as post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Ang Hakbang 4 ay kung saan aktwal na binubuo ang MPF. Kahit na *kinakalkula* dito ang mga coefficients na $x_j$ (at, para sa dynamic variant, maaaring maging masinsinan ang kalkulasyong ito), sa konsepto ito ay isang klasikal na recipe para pagsamahin ang mga quantum measurements mula sa Hakbang 3 sa isang naitamang expectation value &mdash; kaya't itinuturing natin ang buong coefficient at combination workflow bilang post-processing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To assess how well the MPF tracks the true dynamics, we first compute the exact time-evolved expectation values by directly exponentiating the Hamiltonian. This is only tractable because $L = 10$; in the large-scale hardware example below we will have to rely on tensor-network estimates instead.\n"
msgstr "Upang tasahin kung gaano kahusay sinusubaybayan ng MPF ang tunay na dynamics, kalkulahin muna natin ang eksaktong time-evolved expectation values sa pamamagitan ng direktang pag-exponentiate ng Hamiltonian. Ito ay magagawa lamang dahil $L = 10$; sa malaking halimbawa gamit ang hardware sa ibaba, kailangan nating umasa sa tensor-network estimates sa halip.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Static MPF coefficients {#static-mpf-coefficients}"
msgstr "Mga static na MPF coefficient {#static-mpf-coefficients}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Static MPFs use coefficients $x_j$ that are independent of the evolution time, the Hamiltonian, and the initial state. We set up the linear system $Ax = b$ described in the Background and solve for the coefficients. The matrix $A$ is determined by the Trotter step counts $k_j$, the order $\\chi$ of the product formula, and whether the formula is symmetric (which controls the exponents $\\eta_n$).\n"
msgstr "Ang static MPFs ay gumagamit ng coefficients na $x_j$ na independiyente sa oras ng ebolusyon, ang Hamiltonian, at ang paunang estado. Itinatakda natin ang linear system na $Ax = b$ na inilarawan sa Background at nireresolba para sa coefficients. Ang matrix na $A$ ay tinutukoy ng Trotter step counts na $k_j$, ang order $\\chi$ ng product formula, at kung ang formula ay symmetric (na kumokontrol sa exponents na $\\eta_n$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For our small-scale example we use $k_j = [1, 2, 4]$ with a non-symmetric order-$2\\chi=2$ Suzuki-Trotter formula (so $\\chi=1$ and $\\eta_n = 2 + n$, giving $\\eta_0 = 2,\\, \\eta_1 = 3$). The system becomes:\n"
msgstr "Para sa ating maliit na halimbawa, ginagamit natin ang $k_j = [1, 2, 4]$ na may non-symmetric order-$2\\chi=2$ Suzuki-Trotter formula (kaya $\\chi=1$ at $\\eta_n = 2 + n$, ibinibigay ang $\\eta_0 = 2,\\, \\eta_1 = 3$). Ang system ay nagiging:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A =\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 & 1\\\\\n"
"1 & \\frac{1}{2^2} & \\frac{1}{4^2}  \\\\\n"
"1 & \\frac{1}{2^3} & \\frac{1}{4^3}  \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"b =\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A =\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 & 1\\\\\n"
"1 & \\frac{1}{2^2} & \\frac{1}{4^2}  \\\\\n"
"1 & \\frac{1}{2^3} & \\frac{1}{4^3}  \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"b =\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first row enforces unbiasedness ($\\sum_j x_j = 1$); the second and third rows cancel the leading $1/k^2$ and next-order $1/k^3$ Trotter-error terms, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Ang unang row ay nagpapatupad ng unbiasedness ($\\sum_j x_j = 1$); ang ikalawa at ikatlong row ay kina-cancel ang unang-orden na $1/k^2$ at next-order na $1/k^3$ Trotter-error terms, ayon sa pagkakasunod-sunod.\n"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the LSE {#set-up-the-lse}"
msgstr "Itakda ang LSE {#set-up-the-lse}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use `setup_static_lse` from `qiskit_addon_mpf.static` to assemble the matrix $A$ and right-hand-side vector $b$ described above. The matrix $A$ depends not only on $k_j$ but also on our choice of product formula &mdash; in particular its *order* $\\chi$ and whether it is *symmetric*. The `symmetric` flag controls the exponent pattern $\\eta_n$ (symmetric formulas only produce even-power Trotter-error terms; see Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references)). Note that, as shown in Ref. [\\[2\\]](#references), setting `symmetric=True` is not strictly necessary even when the underlying PF is symmetric &mdash; the non-symmetric LSE remains valid (it enforces extra unneeded constraints).\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit natin ang `setup_static_lse` mula sa `qiskit_addon_mpf.static` upang buuin ang matrix na $A$ at right-hand-side vector na $b$ na inilarawan sa itaas. Ang matrix na $A$ ay nakadepende hindi lang sa $k_j$ kundi pati na rin sa ating pinili na product formula &mdash; partikular na sa *order* nitong $\\chi$ at kung ito ay *symmetric*. Ang `symmetric` flag ay kumokontrol sa exponent pattern na $\\eta_n$ (ang symmetric formulas ay gumagawa lamang ng even-power Trotter-error terms; tingnan ang Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references)). Tandaan na, tulad ng ipinapakita sa Ref. [\\[2\\]](#references), ang pagtatakda ng `symmetric=True` ay hindi mahigpit na kinakailangan kahit symmetric ang underlying PF &mdash; ang non-symmetric LSE ay nananatiling valid (nagpapatupad ito ng ekstrang di-kailangang constraints).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For our example we have already set `order = 2` and `symmetric = False` in Step 1.\n"
msgstr "Para sa ating halimbawa, naitakda na natin ang `order = 2` at `symmetric = False` sa Hakbang 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect the constructed matrix $A$ and vector $b$ to confirm they match the system written above.\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang binuong matrix na $A$ at vector na $b$ upang kumpirmahin na tumutugma ang mga ito sa system na isinulat sa itaas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the LSE in hand, we solve for the static coefficients $x_j$ via `lse.solve()` (this is the direct $x = A^{-1}b$ solution).\n"
msgstr "Taglay ang LSE, nireresolba natin ang static coefficients na $x_j$ sa pamamagitan ng `lse.solve()` (ito ang direktang solusyong $x = A^{-1}b$).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize for $x$ using an exact model {#optimize-for-x-using-an-exact-model}"
msgstr "I-optimize ang $x$ gamit ang isang eksaktong modelo {#optimize-for-x-using-an-exact-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively to computing $x = A^{-1}b$, you can use [setup\\_exact\\_model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.static.setup_exact_model.html) to construct a [cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem) instance that uses the LSE as constraints and whose optimal solution will yield $x$.\n"
msgstr "Bilang alternatibo sa pagkalkula ng $x = A^{-1}b$, maaari mo ring gamitin ang [setup\\_exact\\_model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/stubs/qiskit_addon_mpf.static.setup_exact_model.html) upang itayo ang isang [cvxpy.Problem](https://www.cvxpy.org/api_reference/cvxpy.problems.html#cvxpy.Problem) instance na gumagamit ng LSE bilang mga constraint at ang optimal na solusyon nito ay magbubunga ng $x$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize for $x$ using an approximate model {#optimize-for-x-using-an-approximate-model}"
msgstr "I-optimize ang $x$ gamit ang isang tinantyang modelo {#optimize-for-x-using-an-approximate-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It might happen that the $L_1$ norm for the chosen set of $k_j$ values is deemed too high. If that is the case and you cannot choose a different set of $k_j$ values, you can use an approximate solution that constrains the $L_1$-norm to a chosen threshold while minimizing $\\|Ax - b\\|$. Check out the guide on [How to use the approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"
msgstr "Maaaring mangyari na ang $L_1$ norm para sa piniling hanay ng mga halaga ng $k_j$ ay masyadong mataas. Kung ganoon ang kaso at hindi ka makapipili ng ibang hanay ng mga halaga ng $k_j$, maaari kang gumamit ng tinantyang solusyon na naghihigpit sa $L_1$-norm sa isang piniling threshold habang minimisado ang $\\|Ax - b\\|$. Tingnan ang gabay sa [Paano gamitin ang approximate model](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mpf/how_tos/using_approximate_model.html).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic MPF coefficients {#dynamic-mpf-coefficients}"
msgstr "Dynamic MPF coefficients {#dynamic-mpf-coefficients}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The static MPF cancels Trotter-error terms in a Hamiltonian- and state-agnostic way, so it does not necessarily produce the smallest possible approximation error for a given Hamiltonian and initial state. The dynamic MPF (Refs. [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references)) instead finds time-dependent coefficients $x_i(t)$ that minimize the Frobenius-norm distance $\\|\\rho(t) - \\mu^D(t)\\|_F^2$ at each time $t$. As shown in the Background, this requires the overlap matrix $M_{ij}(t)$ between Trotter-evolved states and the overlap $L_i(t)$ with the exact state &mdash; both of which we estimate using tensor-network (TeNPy) backends in `qiskit_addon_mpf`.\n"
msgstr "Ang static MPF ay kina-cancel ang Trotter-error terms sa paraang agnostiko sa Hamiltonian at estado, kaya hindi nito palaging naiibigay ang pinakamaliit na posibleng approximation error para sa isang ibinigay na Hamiltonian at paunang estado. Sa halip, ang dynamic MPF (Refs. [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references)) ay naghahanap ng time-dependent coefficients na $x_i(t)$ na minimisado ang Frobenius-norm distance na $\\|\\rho(t) - \\mu^D(t)\\|_F^2$ sa bawat oras na $t$. Tulad ng ipinapakita sa Background, ito ay nangangailangan ng overlap matrix na $M_{ij}(t)$ sa pagitan ng mga Trotter-evolved states at ang overlap na $L_i(t)$ sa eksaktong estado &mdash; kapwa tinatantiya natin gamit ang tensor-network (TeNPy) backends sa `qiskit_addon_mpf`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To set up the dynamic LSE we need three ingredients:\n"
msgstr "Upang itakda ang dynamic LSE, kailangan natin ng tatlong sangkap:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **approximate evolver factory** that the addon will run for each $k_j$ to produce $\\rho_{k_j}(t)$ as an MPS/MPO. We build it from the layered structure of the order-$2$ Trotter circuit (one layer per `slice_by_depth`), wrapped as a `LayerwiseEvolver` with TeNPy truncation parameters.\n"
msgstr "Isang **approximate evolver factory** na papatakbuhin ng addon para sa bawat $k_j$ upang bumuo ng $\\rho_{k_j}(t)$ bilang MPS/MPO. Binubuo natin ito mula sa layered structure ng order-$2$ Trotter circuit (isang layer bawat `slice_by_depth`), na na-wrap bilang `LayerwiseEvolver` na may TeNPy truncation parameters.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **exact evolver factory** that produces a high-accuracy reference $\\rho(t)$. We use a small-time-step fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter circuit (`dt=0.1`, `order=4`) as a proxy for exact evolution.\n"
msgstr "Isang **exact evolver factory** na gumagawa ng mataas-ang-accuracy na reference na $\\rho(t)$. Ginagamit natin ang isang small-time-step fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter circuit (`dt=0.1`, `order=4`) bilang proxy para sa eksaktong ebolusyon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **identity factory** and an **initial-state MPS** that seed the TeNPy simulation.\n"
msgstr "Isang **identity factory** at isang **initial-state MPS** na nagsisimula ng TeNPy simulation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cell below constructs the approximate evolver factory.\n"
msgstr "Ang cell sa ibaba ay bumubuo ng approximate evolver factory.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\">\n"
"  The options of `LayerwiseEvolver` that determine the details of the tensor network simulation must be chosen carefully to avoid setting up an ill-defined optimization problem.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"We approximate the exact time-evolved state with a fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter formula using a small time step `dt=0.1`. The TeNPy truncation parameters can affect accuracy, so it is important to explore a range of values.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we define an `identity_factory` that yields the initial MPO state and prepare the Néel initial state as an MPS that matches the lattice used by the layered Trotter model.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, tinatakda natin ang isang `identity_factory` na gumagawa ng paunang MPO state at inihahanda ang Néel initial state bilang MPS na tumutugma sa lattice na ginamit ng layered Trotter model.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the factories in place we now compute the dynamic coefficients at each evolution time. For each $t$, `setup_dynamic_lse` builds the relevant overlap matrices via TeNPy, and `setup_frobenius_problem` returns a `cvxpy.Problem` that minimizes the Frobenius-norm cost. The solver returns coefficients $x_j(t)$ tailored to that time; we collect them in `mpf_dynamic_coeffs_list`. If the solver fails for a given $t$, we fall back to zero coefficients so the loop continues.\n"
msgstr "Taglay ang mga factory, kinakalkula natin ngayon ang dynamic coefficients sa bawat oras ng ebolusyon. Para sa bawat $t$, ang `setup_dynamic_lse` ay bumubuo ng kaugnay na overlap matrices sa pamamagitan ng TeNPy, at ang `setup_frobenius_problem` ay nagbabalik ng `cvxpy.Problem` na minimisado ang Frobenius-norm cost. Ang solver ay nagbabalik ng coefficients na $x_j(t)$ na naangkop para sa oras na iyon; tinitipon natin ang mga ito sa `mpf_dynamic_coeffs_list`. Kung nabigo ang solver para sa isang ibinigay na $t$, bumabalik tayo sa zero coefficients upang magpatuloy ang loop.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combine Trotter expectation values with the MPF coefficients {#combine-trotter-expectation-values-with-the-mpf-coefficients}"
msgstr "Pagsamahin ang Trotter expectation values sa MPF coefficients {#combine-trotter-expectation-values-with-the-mpf-coefficients}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we evaluate $\\langle A \\rangle_{\\text{MPF}}(t) = \\sum_j x_j \\, \\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t)$ for each set of coefficients (static-exact, static-approximate, and dynamic), propagate the per-circuit standard errors, and plot the resulting time series against the exact-diagonalization curve.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay ini-evaluate natin ang $\\langle A \\rangle_{\\text{MPF}}(t) = \\sum_j x_j \\, \\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}(t)$ para sa bawat hanay ng coefficients (static-exact, static-approximate, at dynamic), ipinapalaganap ang per-circuit standard errors, at ini-plot ang resultang time series laban sa exact-diagonalization curve.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/multi-product-formula/extracted-outputs/35042576-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/multi-product-formula/extracted-outputs/35042576-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plot above illustrates the interplay between Trotter error and sampling error.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng plot sa itaas ang interplay sa pagitan ng Trotter error at sampling error.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trotter error.** The individual product formulas (grey markers) deviate from the exact curve more and more as time grows. The $k=1$ circuit has the largest deviation and is the shallowest, but it is also already in the regime where $t/k \\gtrsim 1$, so the leading $1/k^{2}$ error term is large. The MPF combinations (colored markers) cancel several of these leading Trotter-error terms, so they track the exact curve much more closely than any single $k_j$ circuit. The remaining gap reflects the higher-order Trotter terms that the MPF does *not* cancel: an order-$2$, $r=3$ static MPF only kills the first two error orders, and at large $t/k_{\\min}$ the uncanceled tail eventually dominates &mdash; so MPF does not guarantee that very shallow circuits remain accurate at arbitrary times.\n"
msgstr "**Trotter error.** Ang mga indibidwal na product formulas (kulay-abong markers) ay lumihis sa eksaktong curve nang lumihis nang lumihis habang tumataas ang oras. Ang $k=1$ circuit ay may pinakamalaking paglihis at ito ang pinakamababaw, ngunit nasa regime na rin kung saan $t/k \\gtrsim 1$, kaya malaki ang unang $1/k^{2}$ error term. Ang mga kombinasyon ng MPF (mga markers na may kulay) ay kina-cancel ang ilan sa mga leading Trotter-error terms na ito, kaya't mas malapit silang sumusubaybay sa eksaktong curve kaysa sa alinmang solong circuit na $k_j$. Ang natitirang agwat ay sumasalamin sa higher-order Trotter terms na *hindi* kina-cancel ng MPF: ang isang order-$2$, $r=3$ static MPF ay pinapatay lamang ang unang dalawang error orders, at sa malaking $t/k_{\\min}$ ay unti-unting nangingibabaw ang di-nakansel na tail &mdash; kaya't hindi ginagarantiya ng MPF na mananatiling tumpak ang napakababaw na circuits sa kahit anong oras.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sampling error.** The wider error bars on the MPF curves are a direct consequence of the linear combination: propagating independent per-circuit standard errors $\\sigma_{k_j}$ gives a total variance $\\sigma_{\\text{MPF}}^2 = \\sum_j x_j^2 \\, \\sigma_{k_j}^2$. Therefore, the larger the $\\|x\\|_2$ (and in practice the $\\|x\\|_1$, which is what we control), the more shots are required to reach a given target uncertainty. This is the trade-off behind the approximate-solver option in the Background: we cap $\\|x\\|_1$ to keep this overhead manageable. Crucially, unlike Trotter error, sampling error shrinks with $1/\\sqrt{N_{\\text{shots}}}$, so it can always be reduced by spending more shots.\n"
msgstr "**Sampling error.** Ang mas malalapad na error bars sa MPF curves ay direktang bunga ng linear combination: ang pagpapalaganap ng independiyenteng per-circuit standard errors na $\\sigma_{k_j}$ ay nagbibigay ng kabuuang variance na $\\sigma_{\\text{MPF}}^2 = \\sum_j x_j^2 \\, \\sigma_{k_j}^2$. Kaya, kung mas malaki ang $\\|x\\|_2$ (at sa praktika ang $\\|x\\|_1$, na siyang kinokontrol natin), mas maraming shots ang kailangan upang maabot ang isang target na uncertainty. Ito ang trade-off sa likod ng opsyong approximate-solver sa Background: hinihigpitan natin ang $\\|x\\|_1$ upang mapanatiling manageable ang overhead na ito. Mahalagang tandaan, hindi tulad ng Trotter error, ang sampling error ay bumababa kasama ng $1/\\sqrt{N_{\\text{shots}}}$, kaya't palagi itong maaaring bawasan sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mas maraming shots.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the large-scale hardware example below, hardware noise enters as an additional error source on each $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$, which similarly gets amplified by the MPF coefficients. We will see how error mitigation interacts with MPFs in that section.\n"
msgstr "Sa malaking halimbawa gamit ang hardware sa ibaba, ang hardware noise ay pumapasok bilang karagdagang error source sa bawat $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$, na katulad ding pinapalakas ng MPF coefficients. Makikita natin kung paano nag-i-interact ang error mitigation sa MPFs sa seksyong iyon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Malaking halimbawa gamit ang hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section we scale the problem up beyond what is possible to simulate exactly. We reproduce some of the results shown in Ref. [\\[3\\]](#references), using a 50-qubit XXZ chain at time $t = 3$. We follow the same four-step workflow as the small-scale example, now targeting real quantum hardware with error mitigation. As in the template, each step is marked inline in the code, and a single step can span multiple cells when its intermediate outputs are worth inspecting.\n"
"The mapping mirrors the small-scale example: define a Hamiltonian, choose Trotter parameters, compute MPF coefficients (static and dynamic), and build circuits. The key differences are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa seksyong ito, pinalalaki natin ang problema lampas sa kung ano ang posibleng simulahin nang eksakto. Ginagaya natin ang ilan sa mga resulta na ipinakita sa Ref. [\\[3\\]](#references), gamit ang isang 50-qubit XXZ chain sa oras na $t = 3$. Sinusundan natin ang parehong four-step workflow ng maliit na halimbawa, ngayon ay tina-target ang tunay na quantum hardware na may error mitigation. Tulad ng sa template, bawat hakbang ay minarkahan inline sa code, at maaaring sumaklaw ang isang solong hakbang sa maraming cells kapag karapat-dapat suriin ang mga intermediate outputs nito.\n"
"Ang mapping ay sumasalamin sa maliit na halimbawa: magtakda ng Hamiltonian, pumili ng Trotter parameters, kalkulahin ang MPF coefficients (static at dynamic), at bumuo ng circuits. Ang mga pangunahing pagkakaiba ay:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **XXZ Hamiltonian** on 50 sites with random couplings drawn from $\\mathcal{U}(0.5, 1.5)$ (Ref. [\\[3\\]](#references)).\n"
msgstr "Isang **XXZ Hamiltonian** sa 50 sites na may random na couplings na kinuha mula sa $\\mathcal{U}(0.5, 1.5)$ (Ref. [\\[3\\]](#references)).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **symmetric** second-order Trotter formula with $k_j = [3, 4, 6]$ (so $\\chi=1$, `symmetric=True`).\n"
msgstr "Isang **symmetric** na second-order Trotter formula na may $k_j = [3, 4, 6]$ (kaya $\\chi=1$, `symmetric=True`).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single fixed evolution time $t = 3$. With $k_{\\min}=3$ this gives $t/k_{\\min}=1$, keeping the shallow constituents inside the Trotter-convergence regime where the leading-error model the MPF relies on is valid.\n"
msgstr "Isang solong nakapirming oras ng ebolusyon na $t = 3$. Sa $k_{\\min}=3$ ito ay nagbibigay ng $t/k_{\\min}=1$, na nagpapanatili sa mababaw na sangkap sa loob ng Trotter-convergence regime kung saan valid ang leading-error model na inaasahan ng MPF.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An additional **single-circuit comparison run with $k = 10$ Trotter steps**, used as a baseline. We chose $k = 10$ because its two-qubit depth on hardware is deeper than the deepest MPF constituent ($k_{\\max}=6$) plus the overhead of running multiple MPF circuits &mdash; deep enough to be noise-limited, which is the regime in which the MPF combination is expected to outperform the single-circuit baseline. It is a \"single deep circuit\" comparison against the MPF combination, not a circuit that targets the MPF's effective Trotter error (which would require many more steps).\n"
msgstr "Isang karagdagang **single-circuit comparison run na may $k = 10$ Trotter steps**, na ginamit bilang baseline. Pinili natin ang $k = 10$ dahil ang two-qubit depth nito sa hardware ay mas malalim kaysa sa pinakamalalim na sangkap ng MPF ($k_{\\max}=6$) kasama ang overhead ng pagpapatakbo ng maraming MPF circuits &mdash; sapat na malalim upang maging noise-limited, na siyang regime kung saan inaasahang mas magiging mahusay ang kombinasyon ng MPF kaysa sa single-circuit baseline. Ito ay isang paghahambing na \"single deep circuit\" laban sa kombinasyon ng MPF, hindi circuit na tina-target ang epektibong Trotter error ng MPF (na mangangailangan ng mas maraming steps).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that even though we are still in Step 1 here (mapping and circuit construction), we also pre-compute the dynamic coefficients alongside the static ones in this cell. Dynamic coefficients depend on $H$ and $t$ but not on the quantum measurements, so they can be computed any time before Step 4. We do it now to keep all the MPF-specific setup in one place.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na kahit nasa Hakbang 1 pa tayo dito (mapping at pagbuo ng circuit), kinakalkula na rin natin nang paunang ang dynamic coefficients kasabay ng static ones sa cell na ito. Ang dynamic coefficients ay nakadepende sa $H$ at $t$ ngunit hindi sa mga quantum measurements, kaya maaari silang kalkulahin anumang oras bago ang Hakbang 4. Ginagawa natin ito ngayon upang mapanatili ang lahat ng MPF-specific na setup sa isang lugar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now optimize the circuits for the chosen backend. We use the Qiskit preset pass manager at `optimization_level=3`, which automatically selects a good set of physical qubits and routes each circuit onto the device topology.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay ino-optimize natin ang mga circuit para sa piniling backend. Ginagamit natin ang Qiskit preset pass manager sa `optimization_level=3`, na awtomatikong pumipili ng magandang hanay ng physical qubits at ni-ru-route ang bawat circuit patungo sa device topology.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running deeper circuits on real hardware requires aggressive error mitigation. We enable dynamical decoupling, gate and measurement twirling, measurement error mitigation, and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE). Note that the ZNE noise factors we use here (`1, 1.2, 1.4`) are smaller than in a shallow-circuit scenario, since the deeper MPF constituents are already close to the noise threshold and large noise amplifications would push them past the point where ZNE extrapolation is reliable.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpapatakbo ng mas malalim na circuits sa tunay na hardware ay nangangailangan ng agresibong error mitigation. Pinapagana natin ang dynamical decoupling, gate at measurement twirling, measurement error mitigation, at zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE). Tandaan na ang mga ZNE noise factors na ginamit dito (`1, 1.2, 1.4`) ay mas maliit kaysa sa isang shallow-circuit scenario, dahil ang mas malalim na sangkap ng MPF ay malapit na sa noise threshold at ang malalaking noise amplifications ay maaaring itulak sila lampas sa punto kung saan reliable pa ang ZNE extrapolation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We submit all four circuits (three MPF constituents at $k_j = [3, 4, 6]$ plus the $k = 10$ baseline) in a single Estimator job.\n"
msgstr "Isinusumite natin ang lahat ng apat na circuits (tatlong MPF constituents sa $k_j = [3, 4, 6]$ kasama ang $k = 10$ baseline) sa isang solong Estimator job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We pull the per-circuit expectation values and standard deviations from the job result, then combine them with each set of MPF coefficients exactly as in the small-scale example: $\\langle A \\rangle_{\\text{MPF}} = \\sum_j x_j \\, \\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$, with propagated variance $\\sigma^2 = \\sum_j x_j^2 \\sigma_{k_j}^2$.\n"
msgstr "Kinukuha natin ang per-circuit expectation values at standard deviations mula sa resulta ng job, at pagkatapos ay pinagsasama natin ang mga ito sa bawat hanay ng MPF coefficients nang eksaktong tulad ng sa maliit na halimbawa: $\\langle A \\rangle_{\\text{MPF}} = \\sum_j x_j \\, \\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$, na may pinalaganap na variance na $\\sigma^2 = \\sum_j x_j^2 \\sigma_{k_j}^2$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/multi-product-formula/extracted-outputs/64360d85-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/multi-product-formula/extracted-outputs/64360d85-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A few observations about the hardware results above:\n"
msgstr "Ilang obserbasyon tungkol sa mga resulta ng hardware sa itaas:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Going deeper is not free on hardware.** The single-circuit baselines tell the story directly: the $k = 6$ circuit is essentially exact ($-0.256$ versus the reference $-0.244$), yet the deeper $k = 10$ baseline is *worse* ($-0.061$, off by $\\sim 0.18$), not better. Once the Trotter error is already small, adding steps mostly deepens the circuit and accumulates more gate noise and decoherence. This is precisely the regime MPFs are built for: reach the accuracy of a deep circuit using only shallow constituents.\n"
msgstr "**Ang paglalim ay hindi libre sa hardware.** Direktang ipinapakita ito ng single-circuit baselines: ang $k = 6$ circuit ay halos eksakto ($-0.256$ laban sa reference na $-0.244$), gayunpaman ang mas malalim na $k = 10$ baseline ay *mas masahol* ($-0.061$, off by $\\sim 0.18$), hindi mas mahusay. Kapag maliit na ang Trotter error, ang pagdagdag ng steps ay pangunahing nagpapalalim lamang ng circuit at nagpapatipon ng mas maraming gate noise at decoherence. Ito mismo ang regime na para dito binuo ang MPFs: maabot ang katumpakan ng isang malalim na circuit gamit lamang ang mababaw na sangkap.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A small-norm MPF beats the deep single circuit.** The approximate-static MPF (capped at $\\|x\\|_1 \\approx 2$) lands at $-0.259$, within $\\sim 0.015$ of the reference and far closer than the $k = 10$ baseline. The dynamic MPF ($-0.127$) also comfortably beats that baseline. Both combine only the shallow $k_j = [3, 4, 6]$ circuits, yet recover an answer the deep single circuit could not.\n"
msgstr "**Isang maliit-ang-norm na MPF ay natatalo ang malalim na single circuit.** Ang approximate-static MPF (hinihigpitan sa $\\|x\\|_1 \\approx 2$) ay napunta sa $-0.259$, sa loob ng $\\sim 0.015$ mula sa reference at mas malapit kaysa sa $k = 10$ baseline. Ang dynamic MPF ($-0.127$) ay komportable ring natatalo ang baseline na iyon. Pareho silang pinagsasama lamang ang mababaw na $k_j = [3, 4, 6]$ circuits, ngunit nabawi ang isang sagot na hindi kayang makuha ng malalim na single circuit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Coefficient norm matters more than mathematical optimality.** The exact-static MPF has $\\|x\\|_1 = 4.66$ and is the *worst* estimator of all ($-0.567$, off by more than $0.3$): the large coefficient norm amplifies the residual gate noise, decoherence, and ZNE error on each $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$ by roughly the same factor, overwhelming the Trotter-error cancellation it buys. Capping the norm (the approximate-static solver, $\\|x\\|_1 \\approx 2$) removes this overwhelm and gives the best estimate &mdash; even though its coefficients no longer cancel the leading Trotter error exactly.\n"
msgstr "**Ang norm ng coefficient ay mas mahalaga kaysa sa mathematical optimality.** Ang exact-static MPF ay may $\\|x\\|_1 = 4.66$ at ito ang *pinakamasahol* na estimator sa lahat ($-0.567$, off by more than $0.3$): ang malaking coefficient norm ay pinapalakas ang natitirang gate noise, decoherence, at ZNE error sa bawat $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$ nang halos parehong salik, na natatabunan ang pagkansel ng Trotter-error na binibili nito. Ang paghihigpit sa norm (ang approximate-static solver, $\\|x\\|_1 \\approx 2$) ay inaalis ang pagkatabunan na ito at nagbibigay ng pinakamahusay na estimate &mdash; kahit hindi na eksaktong kina-cancel ng coefficients nito ang leading Trotter error.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Individual shallow circuits can still be competitive.** The lone $k = 6$ constituent ($-0.256$) is itself essentially exact here &mdash; on this run it is even marginally closer than the approximate-static MPF. The catch is that you do not know in advance *which* single $k$ sits in the sweet spot of \"converged but not yet noise-limited,\" and the safe-looking choice of simply going deeper ($k = 10$) to guarantee Trotter convergence is exactly the one that fails. The MPF gives a principled combination of shallow circuits that does not require guessing the right depth.\n"
msgstr "**Ang mga indibidwal na mababaw na circuit ay maaari pa ring maging competitive.** Ang nag-iisang $k = 6$ na sangkap ($-0.256$) ay halos eksakto na rin dito &mdash; sa run na ito, ito ay bahagyang mas malapit pa kaysa sa approximate-static MPF. Ang problema ay hindi mo alam nang maaga kung *aling* solong $k$ ang nasa sweet spot ng \"converged pero hindi pa noise-limited,\" at ang mukhang-ligtas na pagpipiliang basta pinalalim lang ($k = 10$) upang garantiyahan ang Trotter convergence ay eksaktong ang nabibigo. Ang MPF ay nagbibigay ng makatwirang kombinasyon ng mababaw na circuits na hindi nangangailangan ng paghula sa tamang lalim.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The practical takeaway is that on hardware, MPFs should be paired with strong error mitigation on each individual $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$, the coefficient $L_1$-norm should be kept modest (use the approximate solver, or the dynamic MPF), and the Trotter steps $k_j$ should be chosen so that $t/k_{\\min} \\lesssim 1$ &mdash; here $k_{\\min} = 3$ at $t = 3$ gives $t/k_{\\min} = 1$, keeping the constituents inside the convergent regime where the leading-error model the static MPF relies on is valid. With those choices, the small-norm MPFs here match a converged single circuit while the naive \"just go deeper\" baseline does not, recovering the depth-versus-accuracy advantage shown in Ref. [\\[3\\]](#references). Note also that individual runs are noisy &mdash; on a different submission of the same job (or a different backend), the exact ordering can shift; the robust trends are that small-$\\|x\\|_1$ MPFs do well, the large-$\\|x\\|_1$ exact-static MPF is amplified by hardware noise, and the over-deep single circuit is noise-limited.\n"
msgstr "Ang praktikal na aral ay sa hardware, ang MPFs ay dapat ipares sa malakas na error mitigation sa bawat indibidwal na $\\langle A \\rangle_{k_j}$, ang $L_1$-norm ng coefficient ay dapat panatilihing katamtaman (gumamit ng approximate solver, o ng dynamic MPF), at ang Trotter steps na $k_j$ ay dapat piliin upang $t/k_{\\min} \\lesssim 1$ &mdash; dito ang $k_{\\min} = 3$ sa $t = 3$ ay nagbibigay ng $t/k_{\\min} = 1$, na pinananatili ang mga sangkap sa loob ng convergent regime kung saan valid ang leading-error model na inaasahan ng static MPF. Sa mga pagpipiliang iyon, ang small-norm MPFs dito ay tumutugma sa isang converged single circuit habang ang naive na \"basta pinalalim lang\" baseline ay hindi, na nabawi ang bentaha sa depth-versus-accuracy na ipinakita sa Ref. [\\[3\\]](#references). Tandaan din na ang mga indibidwal na run ay maingay &mdash; sa ibang submission ng parehong job (o ibang backend), maaaring magbago ang eksaktong pagkakasunod-sunod; ang matatag na trends ay ang small-$\\|x\\|_1$ MPFs ay gumaganda, ang large-$\\|x\\|_1$ exact-static MPF ay pinapalakas ng hardware noise, at ang over-deep na single circuit ay noise-limited.\n"

